From: Rui Figueira <rfigueira@cloudflare.com>
Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 23:00:42 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 61/62] Lean synthetic italic to the right, not the left

fontique reports faux-italic slant as a positive angle
(Synthesis::skew = 14), which is the correct sign in font space, where
y points up. This transform is applied to the glyph outline in device
space, where y points down, and the flip between the two mirrors a
shear, so every synthetic italic leaned left.

That does more than look wrong. A left-leaning glyph hangs over the
text before it rather than over its own advance, so italic runs
collided with their preceding neighbour. This shows on any page with
an italic in a family that ships no italic face, which includes
monospace fonts such as Noto Sans Mono.

A shear leaves advances untouched either way, so this changes only the
direction of the slant. A synthetic italic still occupies exactly its
upright advance, which keeps it one cell per character in a terminal.
---
 packages/blitz-paint/src/text.rs | 6 ++++--
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/packages/blitz-paint/src/text.rs b/packages/blitz-paint/src/text.rs
index 06a90ddd7..e61c89c1f 100644
--- a/packages/blitz-paint/src/text.rs
+++ b/packages/blitz-paint/src/text.rs
@@ -734,9 +734,11 @@ pub(crate) fn stroke_text<'a>(
                 let metrics = run.font_metrics();
                 let style = glyph_run.style();
                 let synthesis = run.synthesis();
+                // Font-space y points up but device-space y points down, so a
+                // positive font slant needs a negative device-space shear.
                 let glyph_xform = synthesis
                     .skew()
-                    .map(|angle| Affine::skew(angle.to_radians().tan() as f64, 0.0));
+                    .map(|angle| Affine::skew(-angle.to_radians().tan() as f64, 0.0));
 
                 let css_font_size = font_size as f64 / scale;
 
@@ -883,7 +885,7 @@ pub(crate) fn fill_text<'a>(
             let glyph_xform = run
                 .synthesis()
                 .skew()
-                .map(|angle| Affine::skew(angle.to_radians().tan() as f64, 0.0));
+                .map(|angle| Affine::skew(-angle.to_radians().tan() as f64, 0.0));
             let embolden = if FONT_EMBOLDEN_ENABLED {
                 let fs = font_size as f64 / scale;
                 kurbo::Vec2::new((0.015125 * fs).min(0.3), (0.0121 * fs).min(0.3))
